 Doubleday (left) and Alf Harley (right) try their hand at putting snow balls during one of their climbing holidays in the \"Thirties\". Alf Taylor is in the centre.","id":"B172-10","w":"December 1969"},{"f":"crops/B180/B180-p01-cover.jpg","c":"FRONT COVER. The late Alfred A. Harley","id":"B180-01","w":"March 1973"},{"f":"crops/B229/B229-p08-walk-match-battersea-1938.jpg","c":"The caption that goes with this photograph in our archives reads:\n\"Walk Match at Battersea circa 1938. Starters include H.G. Churcher, C.E.Churcher, D.E. Brown, A.A.Harley, F. Jarvis, C.W.Redgrave.\"\nOur first stab at actually naming the faces came up with Don Brown (1), Harry Churcher (7), Charlie Churcher (23), C.W. Redgrave (24) and Alf Harley (behind Brown). However, as others have become involved and have cast their eyes over the picture, we are now not at all sure of anyone except Alf Harley. For instance, we are told that Charlie Churcher did not wear glasses and the chap next to Harry, second from the left, may be Jack Rutland If any reader can help us with more specific details of the race then we would be very pleased to hear from them.","id":"B229-16","w":"February 2001"},{"f":"crops/B174/B174-p21-harley-lockharts-last-case.jpg","c":"* Edward Heath has his music - Alfred Harley has his amateur dramatics - here he is seen in, \"Lockhart's Last Case\" with a strong supporting cast. In the background it looks like Charlie MacLennan (without trousers) taking finger-prints and the immediate foreground are three heads waiting for the chop whilst the amiable assistant \"Tinker\" is being carpeted by the boss.","id":"B174-37","w":"June 1970"},{"f":"crops/B175/B175-p01-alf-harley-cover.jpg","c":"FRONT COVER---Our retiring General Hon. Secretary, ALF HARLEY, who vacates his Chair after a term of office spanning 32 years. See page 8.","id":"B175-01","w":"September 1970"},{"f":"crops/B175/B175-p08-alf-harley.jpg","c":"","id":"B175-13","w":"September 1970"},{"f":"crops/B175/B175-p09-charlie-redgrave-alf-harley-walk-1929.jpg","c":"Charlie Redgrave, \"The Banjulele Boy\", passes Alf Harley only feet from the tape to win the 1929 Boxing Day Walk Handicap.","id":"B175-13","w":"September 1970"},{"f":"crops/B175/B175-p10-alf-harley-chiswick-1933.jpg","c":"Alf Harley (12) competing in the Chiswick Annual Sports----August 1933.","id":"B175-13","w":"September 1970"},{"f":"crops/B175/B175-p11-queen-elizabeth-aaa-championships-1952.jpg","c":"21st JUNE 1952. Five months after her accession to the throne HER MAJESTY QUEEN ELIZABETH II visits the A.A.A. Championships at the White City. On the left is A.A. Harley and to the right The Marquess of Exeter.","id":"B175-13","w":"September 1970"},{"f":"crops/B176/B176-p05-harley-romulus-remus-trophy.jpg","c":"Another milestone in the life of ALF HARLEY is reached during the 1950's when, as Chairman of the London Association of Athletic Clubs, he receives the ROMULUS AND REMUS trophy from the Italians at London's Dorchester Hotel","id":"B176-07","w":"December 1970"},{"f":"crops/B223/B223-p78-queen-aaa-championships.jpg","c":"Left: 21st June 1952. Five months after her accession to the throne Her Majest Queen Elizabeth II visits the A.A.A. Championships at White City. On the left is Belgrave's President A.A. Harley and on the right is A.A.A. President The Marquess of Exeter. Photographer unknown.","id":"B223-152","w":"November 1995"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B148/B148-p02-1933-walkers-garnet-cup.jpg","caption":"1933 BEIGRAVE WALKERS AND THE R.W.A. 'GARNET' CUP OUTSIDE CLUB H.Q. Front Row: (Left to Right)P. Khlopin, W.G.Dodkin, F.H.Elson,S.L.Ring,R.G.Hillier H. Latter. Rear:(Left to Right) L. Storey, A.L.Fletcher, A.A.Harley, R.F.Elson,H.E.Larman, J.E.Field, J.Rathbone, C.H.Speechley, F.W.Thorn, J.C.Bidgood.","source":"B148-02","when":"November 1962"},"x":1,"share":{"d":"Alf Harley in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1961–2007: 27 mentions in 19 issues, 5 race results and 12 photographs. Wrote or reported 18 items.","img":"https://belgravian-images.stephendgardner.workers.dev/belgravian/crops/B180/B180-p01-cover.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/read/share/p-alf-harley.html"},"legend":false}